# Steer a running turn

## Section

Steering queues a correction for the current request. Mock mode holds the
first model response so the correction is accepted before the request closes.
In live mode the same call may finish quickly; a late correction can be
rejected. Change `backend` to `:live` and set `OPENAI_API_KEY` to try it.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

mock =
  if backend == :mock do
    {:ok, pid} =
      Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(
        script: [
          %{reply: {:wait, :held, {:text, "Initial answer"}}},
          %{reply: {:text, "Revised answer"}}
        ],
        observer: self()
      )

    pid
  end

context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define a steerable Agent

```elixir
defmodule Guide.SteerTurn do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_steer_turn"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
      answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default(""),
      messages: Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.schema()
    })

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Use the latest correction before you finish."
      reasoning :react
      memory history: :messages

      controls do
        steering true
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 2
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.steer_turn", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Queue a correction

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.SteerTurn, id: "guide-steer-turn")
{:ok, request} = Guide.SteerTurn.ask(server, "Give a short review.", context: context)

if mock do
  receive do
    {:mock_llm_waiting, ^mock, :held, _worker} -> :ok
  after
    5_000 -> raise "The mock provider did not reach its barrier"
  end
end

steering = Jido.AI.Orchestration.steer(request, "Also mention the tests.")
if mock, do: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.release(mock, :held)
result = Jido.AI.Request.await(request, timeout: 10_000)

%{steering: steering, result: result}
```

In mock mode, steering is queued and the second model call returns the revised
answer. Live mode shows either accepted input or a clean late-input rejection.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [_, _]} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
end

:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Stream, steer, and cancel](../v3/12_stream_steer_cancel.md).
